# Recovery Strategy: Basic Front-End Workflow

## File Purpose

This file provides basic recovery strategies for front-end development tasks. It should be used when:

- Implementation encounters common issues that need resolution
- Basic error patterns need to be addressed
- Implementation was interrupted and needs to be resumed
- Simple UI or state management issues occur
- Standard API integration problems arise

This parameter is designed to work with recovery-focused message-commands, providing structured approaches to recovering from common implementation issues.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains basic recovery strategies and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in message-commands:

```
recovery-strategy: @parameters/front-end/continuation/recovery-strategy-basic.mdc
```

For other recovery approaches, see:
- `recovery-strategy-advanced.md`: For complex architectural recovery
- `recovery-strategy-log-based.md`: For log-driven recovery approaches
- `recovery-strategy-error-recovery.md`: For critical error situations

## Basic Recovery Process Overview

The basic recovery process follows these key steps:

1. **Issue Identification and Assessment**
   - Identify the specific implementation issue
   - Assess the severity and scope
   - Determine affected components
   - Locate relevant code sections

2. **Recovery Strategy Selection**
   - Select appropriate recovery pattern
   - Identify minimal required changes
   - Plan step-by-step recovery approach
   - Prepare verification methods

3. **Recovery Implementation**
   - Apply targeted fixes
   - Make minimal necessary changes
   - Implement standard error handling
   - Add validation as needed

4. **Recovery Verification**
   - Test fixed functionality
   - Verify component behavior
   - Confirm issue resolution
   - Document recovery approach

## Issue Identification and Assessment

Begin by identifying and assessing the implementation issue:

```typescript
// 1. Review implementation progress to identify reported issues
read_file("[planning_folder_path]/implementation-progress.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 2. Check component implementation
read_file("[component_file_path]", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 3. Check component styles if relevant
read_file("[component_style_path]", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 4. Check relevant API integration
grep_search("fetch|axios|api\\.", false, "[component_file_path]")

// 5. Check state management
grep_search("useState|useReducer|useContext", false, "[component_file_path]")
```

## Common Issue Categories

### 1. Prop Handling Issues
- Missing props validation
- Incorrect prop types
- Default prop values missing
- Optional props handling

### 2. State Management Issues
- Incorrect initial state
- Missing state updates
- Improper state dependencies
- Unnecessary re-renders

### 3. API Integration Issues
- Missing error handling
- Incorrect data parsing
- Loading state handling
- API timeout issues

### 4. UI Rendering Issues
- Conditional rendering bugs
- CSS class conflicts
- Layout inconsistencies
- Responsive design issues

### 5. Event Handling Issues
- Missing event handlers
- Event propagation issues
- Form submission problems
- Keyboard accessibility

## Basic Recovery Strategies

### 1. Prop Validation Recovery

```typescript
// Before: Missing prop validation
const Component = ({ data, onAction }) => {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{data.title}</h2>
      <button onClick={onAction}>Action</button>
    </div>
  );
};

// After: With prop validation
import PropTypes from 'prop-types';

const Component = ({ data, onAction }) => {
  // Add default value and null check
  const title = data?.title || 'Untitled';
  
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{title}</h2>
      <button onClick={onAction || (() => {})}>Action</button>
    </div>
  );
};

// PropTypes validation
Component.propTypes = {
  data: PropTypes.shape({
    title: PropTypes.string,
  }),
  onAction: PropTypes.func,
};

// Default props
Component.defaultProps = {
  data: { title: 'Untitled' },
  onAction: () => {},
};
```

### 2. State Management Recovery

```typescript
// Before: Problematic state management
const [items, setItems] = useState([]);

const addItem = (newItem) => {
  items.push(newItem); // Direct mutation!
  setItems(items);
};

// After: Correct state handling
const [items, setItems] = useState([]);

const addItem = (newItem) => {
  setItems(prevItems => [...prevItems, newItem]); // Immutable update
};
```

### 3. API Integration Recovery

```typescript
// Before: Error-prone API call
const fetchData = async () => {
  setLoading(true);
  const response = await fetch(apiUrl);
  const data = await response.json();
  setData(data);
  setLoading(false);
};

// After: With basic error handling
const fetchData = async () => {
  setLoading(true);
  setError(null);
  
  try {
    const response = await fetch(apiUrl);
    
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`API error: ${response.status}`);
    }
    
    const data = await response.json();
    setData(data);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('API error:', error);
    setError('Failed to load data');
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
};
```

### 4. UI Rendering Recovery

```typescript
// Before: Problematic conditional rendering
return (
  <div>
    {isLoading && <Spinner />}
    {data.items.map(item => (
      <Item key={item.id} {...item} />
    ))}
  </div>
);

// After: Safe conditional rendering
return (
  <div>
    {isLoading && <Spinner />}
    {!isLoading && !data && <div>No data available</div>}
    {!isLoading && data && data.items && (
      <>
        {data.items.length === 0 ? (
          <div>No items found</div>
        ) : (
          data.items.map(item => (
            <Item key={item?.id || `item-${Math.random()}`} {...item} />
          ))
        )}
      </>
    )}
  </div>
);
```

### 5. Event Handling Recovery

```typescript
// Before: Problematic event handling
const handleSubmit = () => {
  // Missing event.preventDefault()
  // Form will reload page
  submitData(formData);
};

// After: Correct event handling
const handleSubmit = (event) => {
  event.preventDefault(); // Prevent page reload
  
  // Validate before submitting
  if (!formData.name || !formData.email) {
    setError('Please fill all required fields');
    return;
  }
  
  submitData(formData);
};
```

## Recovery Implementation

Apply recovery strategies systematically:

```typescript
// 1. Understand the component with the issue
read_file("[component_file_path]", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 2. Implement basic recovery strategy
edit_file("[component_file_path]",
          "Apply basic recovery strategy",
          "// ... existing code ...\n\n// Recovery fix: [describe fix]\n// ... implementation code ...")

// 3. Add basic validation if needed
edit_file("[component_file_path]",
          "Add basic validation",
          "// ... existing code ...\n\n// Add validation\nif (!data) {\n  return <div>No data available</div>;\n}\n\n// ... existing code ...")

// 4. Update implementation progress
edit_file("[planning_folder_path]/implementation-progress.md",
          "Update implementation progress with recovery details",
          "// ... existing content ...\n\n## Recovery Progress (Date: [current_date])\n\n### Issues Resolved\n- Fixed: [issue_1] with [approach]\n- Fixed: [issue_2] with [approach]\n- Implemented: Basic validation for [component]\n\n// ... existing content ...")
```

## Recovery Verification

Verify that recovery strategies have resolved the issues:

```typescript
// 1. Run tests to verify fixes
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run test -- --testPathPattern=[component_name]", false)

// 2. Check for type errors
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run type-check", false)

// 3. Create UX situation to verify fix
edit_file("[planning_folder_path]/recovery-verification-ux-situation.md",
          "Create UX situation to verify recovery",
          "# Recovery Verification UX Situation\n\n## Steps to Verify\n\n1. Navigate to [page]\n2. Interact with [component]\n3. Verify [expected behavior]\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n- Component should render correctly\n- Interactions should work as expected\n- No errors should occur")
```

## Common Recovery Patterns by Issue Type

| Issue | Recovery Pattern |
|-------|-----------------|
| Missing prop validation | Add PropTypes or TypeScript interfaces |
| Null/undefined errors | Add null checks and default values |
| State mutation issues | Use immutable update patterns |
| API error handling | Add try/catch and loading/error states |
| Event handler issues | Prevent default actions and add validation |
| Key prop warnings | Implement proper and unique key strategies |
| Conditional rendering | Add explicit checks for all conditions |
| CSS conflicts | Use CSS modules or scoped class names |
| Form submission | Add validation and prevent default submission |

